{
    "map": {
        "description": "Calculates residue errors and the root mean square error (RMSE) based on the coordinates of the input links between known control points to be used for spatial data transformation.",
        "in_link_features.descr": "The input link features that link known control points for spatial transformation.",
        "in_link_features.title": "Input Link Features",
        "method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the transformation method that will be used to convert the input feature coordinates.</p><ul><li><span title=\"AFFINE\">Affine transformation</span>—A minimum of three transformation links is required. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"PROJECTIVE\">Projective transformation</span>—A minimum of four transformation links is required.</li><li><span title=\"SIMILARITY\">Similarity transformation</span>—A minimum of two transformation links is required.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "method.domain.AFFINE": "Affine transformation",
        "method.domain.PROJECTIVE": "Projective transformation",
        "method.domain.SIMILARITY": "Similarity transformation",
        "method.title": "Method",
        "out_link_table.descr": "<xdoc><p>The output table containing the input links feature IDs and their residual errors. The residual errors for input links will be written to the specified output table that contains the following fields:</p><ul><li>Orig_FID—The input link feature ID</li><li>X_Source—The x-coordinate of the source or from the end location of the link</li><li>Y_Source—The y-coordinate of the source or from the end location of the link</li><li>X_Destination—The x-coordinate of the destination or to the end location of the link</li><li>Y_Destination—The y-coordinate of the destination or to the end location of the link</li><li>Residual_Error—The residual error of the transformed location</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "out_link_table.title": "Output Link Table",
        "out_rmse.title": "RMSE",
        "title": "Calculate Transformation Errors"
    }
}
